(7489201, 1178366, 100831, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by herfotoman:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>BTW, you don''t have to count.   They put the valid dates there for us.  :D </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I don''t believe everything I read. Hehe<br/> <br/>My clearly flawed system works like this: <br/>- Take photo''s over the week-end [mostly hastily Sunday-afternoon before the light goes..]<br/>- Do the adjusting Sunday-evening for the week''s challenges, no time in the week for that.<br/> <br/>All weekend-photo''s are fine for the previous week''s challenges, I do not even think about dates. But when a long-weekend or short holiday comes around, I sort-of look at the submission day and sort-of count back that it will work out, so now I''m sort-of in trouble. Just make sure I never become an auditor/accountant by profession....Oh no, too late.<br/> <br/>Thanks again for the good set of comments. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Funny. And who cares. You''d make a great accountant, I''m sure. Will love this post regardless what else you do,</td>', 'Originally posted by herfotoman: Originally posted by Lydia: BTW, you don''t have to count.   They put the valid dates there for us.  :D   I don''t believe everything I read. Hehe My clearly flawed system works like this: - Take photo''s over the week-end [mostly hastily Sunday-afternoon before the light goes..]- Do the adjusting Sunday-evening for the week''s challenges, no time in the week for that. All weekend-photo''s are fine for the previous week''s challenges, I do not even think about dates. But when a long-weekend or short holiday comes around, I sort-of look at the submission day and sort-of count back that it will work out, so now I''m sort-of in trouble. Just make sure I never become an auditor/accountant by profession....Oh no, too late. Thanks again for the good set of comments.   Funny. And who cares. You''d make a great accountant, I''m sure. Will love this post regardless what else you do,', '2016-12-28 23:18:44.000000', NULL, 0);
